1
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:09,100
Let's look at the format that is
needed for your target data.

2
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:13,520
This target data is sometimes also
called categories data or feature

3
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,000
data.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,540
This data may either be a tab in

5
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:20,400
your Google spreadsheet or it may
be a CSV file.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,060
In both cases, the format is the
same.

7
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:27,060
First of all, there are four
important column headers.

8
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:30,320
Category, name, and then min and
max.

9
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:37,120
In the category column, we have
the list of categories that we're

10
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,900
going to use for our targets.

11
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:40,620
So in this case, we've got gender,

12
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:43,220
we've got age bucket, we've got
ethnicity, and we've got

13
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:43,620
disability.

14
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:46,640
Under name, we have each of the

15
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:50,080
possible values that these
categories can take.

16
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:53,780
So for the gender category, our
possible values are female, male,

17
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:55,220
and non -binary or other.

18
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:58,360
And then finally, we have

19
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,630
numerical values, which will be
the minimum and maximum targets

20
00:01:02,630 --> 00:01:04,550
for each of those values.

21
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:07,590
So for instance, in this sample,

22
00:01:07,590 --> 00:01:13,850
we have a minimum of 10 and a
maximum of 11 for the female value

23
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:15,470
of the gender category.

24
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:17,570
Okay, so that's the basic format.

25
00:01:17,570 --> 00:01:22,770
There is one other thing to check.

26
00:01:22,990 --> 00:01:24,430
So in this example, we're

27
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:26,670
imagining that we're going to
select 20 people.

28
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:30,260
It's very important that the sum
of the minimums for each category

29
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:37,460
is less than or equal to 20, and
the sum of the maximums is greater

30
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:38,960
than or equal to 20.

31
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:40,580
Let me show you what I mean.

32
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:44,200
If I highlight all the minimums in
my gender category, then the sum

33
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:48,660
appears down the bottom here, and
that sum is 10 plus 9 plus 0.

34
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:49,620
It's 19.

35
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:52,260
This is less than or equal to 20,

36
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:53,100
so we're okay.

37
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:57,110
If I check again, for the age

38
00:01:57,110 --> 00:01:57,930
bucket minimums, I get 17.

39
00:01:57,930 --> 00:02:00,470
For the ethnicity minimums, I get

40
00:02:00,470 --> 00:02:00,570
17.

41
00:02:00,570 --> 00:02:03,050
And for the disability minimums, I

42
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:03,730
get 19.

43
00:02:03,730 --> 00:02:08,630
All of them were less than or

44
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:11,630
equal to 20, so that's good.

45
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:13,270
Let's check the maximums.

46
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:14,710
For gender, my maximums add up to
22.

47
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:15,650
For age buckets, 23.

48
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:17,570
For ethnicity, 22.

49
00:02:17,570 --> 00:02:21,150
And finally, for disability, the
maximums add up to 21.

50
00:02:21,150 --> 00:02:32,320
So in every single case, the sum
of my maximums was greater than or

51
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:36,040
equal to 20, and so everything is
satisfied.

52
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:39,800
I have what we call coherent
targets, and I am good to go.

